{"label":"convex","explanation":"Let a=11/8. For f(x)=log(1+e^{ax})-(121/1024)x^2, we have
f''(x)=a^2\,\frac{e^{ax}}{(1+e^{ax})^2}-\frac{121}{512}
=\frac{121}{512}\left(8\frac{e^{ax}}{(1+e^{ax})^2}-1\right).
Set t=e^{ax}>0. On x\in[-1,1], t\in[e^{-11/8},e^{11/8}]\approx[0.252,3.955]. The term q(t)=t/(1+t)^2 is maximized at t=1 and decreases as t moves away from 1; thus on this interval its minimum is at the endpoints. At t=e^{-11/8} (and symmetrically e^{11/8}), 8q(t)-1\approx 0.286>0. Hence f''(x)>0 for all x\in[-1,1], so f is convex (and not concave) on the whole interval."}

